# game_data

If a script wrote it, it is not in git.

| Path | Git | Who writes it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `curated/` | yes | a person |
| `generated/docs/` | no | `extract_docs_json.py` from Docs.json |
| `generated/world/` | no | FModel level export |
| `generated/map_highres.png` + tiles | no | `extract_map_image.py` |
| `map/static/map/icons/` | no | `copy_icons.py` |

- `curated/typePaths.json` is what the parser keys behavior off (belts, miners, wires). `pickupItems.json` cannot be recovered from FModel; learn new entries with `extract_collectables.py --items-from-save`.
- Shapes: `SCHEMA.md` for docs tables; each extractor header for world tables. Do not invent a parallel schema in Rust — `gamedata/mod.rs` deserializes these files.
- CI / production archive is **game-data-v3** (v2 has no `world/` split). Unpack with `py game_data/package_game_data.py unpack game_data.zip`.
- `sav_core` will not compile without generated JSON. That is intentional.
